==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|frezzen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|frezzan}}, {{m|goh|firezzan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*fraetan}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vreten}}, {{cog|en|fret}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽}}, {{cog|sv|fräta}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈfʁɛsn̩/}}
* {{audio|de|De-fressen.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|fressen<frisst#fraß,gefressen,fräße>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive|of an animal}} to [[eat]]; to [[feed]] on; to [[devour]]
# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive|of a person|pejorative}} to [[stuff]] oneself; to [[gorge]] oneself; to [[eat]] like a pig
#: {{ux|de|Erst kommt das '''Fressen''', dann kommt die Moral.|First comes the '''stomach''', then comes ethics.}}
# {{lb|de|figurative|chiefly|reflexive}} to [[eat away]] (e.g. metal) {{+obj|de|:durch}}
# {{lb|de|figurative|transitive|}} to [[consume]], to [[guzzle]], to [[burn]] (e.g. fuel, money)
# {{lb|de|transitive|colloquial|perfect only}} to [[despise]], to have a [[pet peeve]] against
#: {{uxi|de|Den hab ich ja '''gefressen!'''|I can’t stand that guy!|lit=I have eaten that one.}}

